            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for mist, then the Malayalam for thunder and lightning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പതുക്കെ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പതുക്കെ (patukke) — \"slowly\". പതുക്കെ പറയൂ (patukke paṟayū) — \"please say it slowly\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പതുക്കെ (patukke) is native Dravidian, from the verb \"to crouch, move stealthily\"; DEDR 3912 lists the root with Tamil patuṅku and Kannada padugu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The most useful request a learner can make."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
