          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഉറക്കെ (uṟakke) is native Dravidian: DEDR 721 lists Malayalam uṟakkē, \"strongly, firmly, aloud\", under the verb \"to be firm\", with Tamil uṟai, \"to become firm\", and Telugu oṟapu, \"firmness\"."
