            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കാത്തിരിക്കൂ (kāttirikkū) — \"please wait\". The ending ‑ഊ (-ū) makes a polite request, as in പറയൂ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കാത്തിരിക്കൂ (kāttirikkū) is native Dravidian, \"sit watching\": a form of the verb \"to guard, watch, wait\" (DEDR 1416, with Tamil kā) joined to the verb \"to sit, to be\" (DEDR 480, with Tamil iru), in its request form."
            }
          ]
        },
